<title>MONACO: TENNIS-LEADING ATP PRIZE-MONEY WINNERS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-LEADING ATP PRIZE-MONEY WINNERS.</headline>
<dateline>MONACO 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading prize-money winners issued</p>
<p>by the ATP Tour on Monday:</p>
<p> 1. Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia)	$1,817,313</p>
<p> 2. Pete Sampras (U.S.)		   1,754,922</p>
<p> 3. Thomas Muster (Austria)	     1,506,566</p>
<p> 4. Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia)	  1,397,355</p>
<p> 5. Michael Chang (U.S.)		  1,374,816</p>
<p> 6. Richard Krajicek (Netherlands)    1,185,511</p>
<p> 7. Andre Agassi (U.S.)		   1,045,660</p>
<p> 8. Todd Woodbridge (Australia)	   939,738</p>
<p> 9. Mark Woodforde (Australia)	    895,982</p>
<p> 10. Wayne Ferreira (South Africa)	879,430</p>
<p> 11. Jakob Hlasek (Switzerland)	   807,128</p>
<p> 12. Marc Rosset (Switzerland)	    784,679</p>
<p> 13. Alberto Costa (Spain)		  742,156</p>
<p> 14. Marcelo Rios (Chile)		   720,148</p>
<p> 15. Paul Haarhuis (Netherlands)	  719,006</p>
<p> 16. Boris Becker (Germany)		 715,427</p>
